Quick Sort:
Quick Sort selects a pivot, partitions the array around the pivot, and recursively sorts the two parts.

Case	      Time Complexity
Best Case	    O(n log n)
Average Case	O(n log n)
Worst Case    	O(n²)
Space Complexity	O(log n) 

Quick Sort is generally very fast in practice.
Its worst case occurs when the pivot repeatedly produces highly unbalanced partitions.
Good pivot selection can greatly reduce the chance of the worst case.
